# Architecture Map: Which Pattern to Use When

| Problem Area | What You Want to Do | Category | Recommended Pattern |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Object Lifecycle** | Create product families that must stay compatible | Creational | **Abstract Factory** |
| | Construct an object with many optional parameters safely | Creational | **Builder** |
| | Avoid expensive re-initialization by duplicating an existing instance | Creational | **Prototype** |
| | Share a single managed service instance across the system | Creational | **Singleton (Container Scope)** |
| **Class Composition** | Make incompatible APIs or libraries work together | Structural | **Adapter** |
| | Add logging, metric tracking, or caching to an existing service transparently | Structural | **Decorator** or **Proxy** |
| | Provide a clean 80/20 public interface to a sprawling subsystem | Structural | **Facade** |
| | Represent hierarchical trees (e.g., UI trees, file directories) uniformly | Structural | **Composite** |
| | Render millions of small objects without exhausting RAM | Structural | **Flyweight** |
| **Control & Communication** | Swap business logic or calculations at runtime | Behavioral | **Strategy** |
| | Broadcast events to multiple subscribers asynchronously | Behavioral | **Observer** |
| | Implement transactional actions, undo buffers, or task queues | Behavioral | **Command** |
| | Process requests through sequential validation and auth filters | Behavioral | **Chain of Responsibility** |
| | Manage complex object state transitions cleanly | Behavioral | **State** |

